all the time!\"\n\nHoping to improve Sieg's smarts and savvy, Nia and her companions secretly devised a plan to construct a learning machine.\nNia programmed the device to use simulations to teach etiquette and administer an electric shock for incorrect answers and responses, then tricked Sieg into accepting it by passing it off as combat support gear. When Sieg put it on, Nia and her companions congratulated themselves on the success of their scheme — while screams of agony echoed from Sieg's room."},"used_in":[{"tip":"Raid: Destroyer Gaze","cat":"pve","banner":"RAID_DG.webp"},{"tip":"Castle Rush: Jave","cat":"pve","banner":"CR_JAVE.webp"},{"tip":"Power Up Dungeon: Earth","cat":"pve","banner":"PU_DUNGEON_EARTH.webp"},{"tip":"Advent Expedition: Kyle","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENT_KYLE.webp"},{"tip":"Power Up Dungeon: Gold","cat":"pve","banner":"PU_DUNGEON_GOLD.webp"},{"tip":"Tower of Trials","cat":"pve","banner":"TOWER_OF_TRIALS.webp"},{"tip":"Adventure (Both)","cat":"pve","banner":"ADVENTURE_BOTH.webp"}],"lore":"While the other Crusaders often wield the power of demons directly, Sieg wields it via his gigantic demonic sword instead.\nSieg is also the one who rescued Shane when her village was attacked by demons.\nHe feels very guilty about the incident; because if his demonic sword had not been acting up in the moment, he probably could've helped sooner and saved many more people.\nHe tries to hide it from Shane by acting even more brash than he usually does when he's around her.\nEspada and the others often put him on blast for being a rude and aggressive oaf with muscles for brains, but he can be quite considerate and thoughtful when it comes to his close friends.\nEspada, Shane, and Ruri are grateful for his presence and enjoy his company more than they'd care to admit.\nThe scars on his body may lead one to think that he employs a reckless fighting style, but those scars are all inflicted by his rebellious demonic blade rather than his actual enemies.\nIn fact, he's actually never been injured by a demon during his time with the Crusaders.\nHe's well-respected in the Crusaders as a whole due to his raw skill."}